id: pm-ntnv4k
title: "GH-1138: linked test name filters can pass after executing zero tests"
description: "Track GitHub issue #1138: linked test commands using runner name filters can exit zero after matching no tests. `pm test <id> --run` records a green receipt even though the evidence command performed no assertions, silently invalidating the durable verification claim after a test rename or typo."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,evidence-integrity,github,linked-tests,tdd
created_at: "2026-08-28T14:43:01.407Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T20:44:38.781Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Add an SDK-owned executed-test assertion primitive and declarative minimum-count field; recognize supported runner receipts without brittle prose-only heuristics; fail zero-test filtered commands closed; preserve explicit non-test smoke commands; add unit, integration, CLI, MCP/schema, history, Node runner, and temp-workspace acceptance coverage."
parent: pm-33cw
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub issue #1138
severity: high
environment: "pm 2026.8.28, Node 26.5.0, Linux; node --test command with --test-name-pattern matching zero tests"
repro_steps: "Link a `node --test --test-name-pattern` command whose pattern matches no test, run it through `pm test <id> --run`, and observe ok true with the runner reporting pass 0."
expected_result: A linked test declares and enforces a minimum executed-test count through a public SDK-owned runner receipt contract; zero-test filtered runs fail closed with actionable evidence.
actual_result: "The child process exits zero, pm reports the linked test passed, and no structured field distinguishes zero executed tests from a real passing assertion."
affected_version: 2026.8.21-2026.8.28
component: linked-tests
regression: true
customer_impact: "Renamed or mistyped test filters silently turn immutable PM verification evidence into a tautology, misleading later agents and release gates."
